README (patch ignores everything above the first "---" line)
=====================================================================
amara-voice-speak.diff: a local "say this line" entry for Amara Voice (Lane C1, 2026-11-14)

Why: Amara Voice only speaks its own replies (and timer/alarm lines). There is no speak/TTS entry:
the level feed (ws 8791) is send-only, logs/state and turns.jsonl are outputs, and the only inbound
signal the app uses is SIGUSR1 (stop speaking, still not in the live loop). Navy mode needs to say one
line, in Amara's own voice (Ming, neosoul_g), only when the look was opened by voice.

What it adds (amara_voice.py only, ~40 lines, stdlib, no new package, no network):
  - speak_watcher thread: polls <amara-voice>/speak/request.json every 0.4 s, reads and deletes it.
  - Request: {"id": "...", "text": "...", "ts": <epoch ms>}. Spoken only if ts is within 15 s, text is
    non-empty (capped at 240 chars, whitespace collapsed) AND the navy flag file
    (<app data>/navy_local_only, written by Amara OS) says "1". Anything else is dropped (fail closed).
  - Speaks through the existing say() under skills.audio_lock (never over a timer or her own reply).
  - Writes its pid to logs/speak_ready at start and removes it at exit. Amara OS treats the speak path
    as READY only when that pid is the running amara_voice.py; otherwise speak() stays unwired.

What Taisun applies (live, non-git dir; the app side is already built and inert until this lands):
  1. cd ~/projects/amara-voice && cp amara_voice.py amara_voice.py.bak-$(date +%F)
  2. patch -p1 --dry-run < ~/projects/nexus-amara/tasks/proposed/amara-voice-speak.diff   (check it applies)
  3. patch -p1 < ~/projects/nexus-amara/tasks/proposed/amara-voice-speak.diff
  4. Restart Amara Voice (Voice panel: Stop, Start, or ./amara stop && ./amara start).
  The navy-gate patch (amara-voice-navy-gate.diff) is separate; this one reads the flag file itself.

How to test (all local, no sound needed until step 3):
  1. ls ~/projects/amara-voice/logs/speak_ready  -> contains the loop's pid; ls -ld speak/ -> 0700.
  2. Navy off: write {"text":"hello","ts":<now epoch ms>} to speak/request.json -> the file vanishes
     within 1 s, nothing is said (flag is not "1").
  3. In Amara OS, say "Amara, navy mode" (voice-opened). She says the caption line in her voice.
     Type the same into chat instead: the look opens, nothing is spoken.
  4. Stop Amara Voice: logs/speak_ready disappears and the app's speak() is unwired again.
Option, not used: macOS /usr/bin/say is local but is NOT Amara's voice; nothing in the voice stack uses it.
